(:id "port/python/vt/reflection" :state :done
 :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_layout_test.go: TestPythonReflectionLayout, TestPythonReflectionLayoutNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_corpus_test.go: TestPythonReflectionCorpus, TestPythonReflectionCorpusNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionVocabularyNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionKindHoleNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionStrictTypes" "internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_layout_test.go: TestPythonReflectionLiveIdentityAndReset, TestPythonReflectionAccessors, TestPythonReflectionAccessorNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionResetLargeArrays, TestPythonReflectionResetLargeArraysNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_docs_test.go: TestPythonReflectionFieldVocabulary, TestPythonReflectionFieldVocabularyNegativeControl" "make/python-reflection.mk: python-reflection, python-reflection-negative-control")
 :tested-revision "7a7d4071d16de05f2cbeb759788186775ae7f192"
 :note "2026-11-17: for every unit of the view corpus and the tables manifest (48 units), the layout each generated descriptor carries (record size, alignment, cook and region columns, every field's offset, pieces, element size and alignment, bounds, vocabulary ids and union arms) equals the compiler's ir.RecordLayout line for line, and the unit view's listing equals the Go view listing (viewlisting.Listing) line for line, under both pinned interpreters; strict mypy is clean over every unit. The controls move Record.value's offset, drop a table row, drift a table doc, an arm doc, a JSON key, a constant, an enum id and a field id in the generated code, and each goes red on its own line. Run on macOS arm64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")

(:id "port/python/vt/doc-tags" :state :done
 :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_docs_test.go: TestPythonReflectionDescriptorDocs, TestPythonReflectionDescriptorDocsNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionAnnotationAgreement, TestPythonReflectionAnnotationAgreementNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionAnnotationEscapes" "internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_corpus_test.go: TestPythonReflectionCorpus, TestPythonReflectionCorpusNegativeControl" "make/python-reflection.mk: python-reflection-negative-control")
 :tested-revision "7a7d4071d16de05f2cbeb759788186775ae7f192"
 :note "2026-11-17: the doc comment and ordered tags of a table, a field and a union arm in the descriptors equal the IR's, quotes, backslashes and non-ASCII text included, and the unit view's rows carry the same annotations as the descriptors they point at; across the corpus every table, type, field, enum, flags and union row's doc and tags equal the Go view listing. The controls drift a table doc, a field doc, the field tag order and an arm doc in the generated module, and each goes red. Run on macOS arm64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")

(:id "port/python/vt/unit-registry" :state :done
 :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_test.go: TestPythonReflection" "internal/codegen/pythontable/reflection_corpus_test.go: TestPythonReflectionCorpus, TestPythonReflectionCorpusNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionViewIsLazy, TestPythonReflectionDetachedVocabularyIDs" "compiler/pythonleg_reflection_on_test.go: TestPythonReflectionDriverCorpus, TestPythonReflectionDriverPacketOnly, TestPythonReflectionDriverNameCollision, TestPythonReflectionDriverNegativeControl, TestPythonReflectionDriverPacketUnionNegativeControl" "make/python-reflection.mk: python-reflection, python-reflection-negative-control")
 :tested-revision "7a7d4071d16de05f2cbeb759788186775ae7f192"
 :note "2026-11-17: UnitView() returns one registry, loaded on first use, over the unit's packet types, tables, constants, enums, flags and unions; for every corpus and manifest unit, packet-only units included, its listing equals the Go view listing under both pinned interpreters, and the public driver emits it for every such unit and refuses a declaration or module named UnitView. Removing the unit_view.py emission turns TestPythonReflection red; the corpus control drops a table row and the listing goes red on it. Run on macOS arm64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
